# ---- Never commit meeting content ----
# Meetings live in ~/Meetings by default, but guard against a stray config,
# a test run pointed at the repo, or a spike writing where it shouldn't.
# These files contain other people's voices and words.
Meetings/
Recordings/
**/.plume/
*.caf
*.m4a
# NOTE: *.wav is deliberately NOT ignored — Phase 2 needs committed WAV/RTTM
# diarization fixtures. Keep real meeting audio out by path, not extension.

# ---- Models (hundreds of MB, re-downloadable) ----
Models/
*.mlmodelc/
*.mlpackage/

# ---- Swift / SPM ----
.build/
.swiftpm/
*.o
*.dSYM/

# ---- Xcode ----
DerivedData/
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserdatad/
build/

# ---- Built products ----
*.app/
*.dmg

# ---- macOS ----
.DS_Store
dist/

# ---- The Homebrew tap is a separate repo, never a directory in this one ----
# `gh repo create sylvainlafitte/homebrew-tap --clone` run from here drops an
# empty clone inside the working tree, and git then refuses to stage *anything*:
# "fatal: 'homebrew-tap/' does not have a commit checked out". Ignoring it means
# a repeat is harmless instead of blocking every commit. Casks/plume.rb here is
# the source of truth; release-cask.sh copies it into a clone kept elsewhere
# (~/src/homebrew-tap by default, or $PLUME_TAP).
homebrew-tap/
